<% slot :hero do %>
  <%= render Hero.new(
    title: "Reporting that no longer eats up the week",
    lede: "As a publicly listed investment association supervised by the Danish
      FSA, Falcon Invest has to keep up with heavy reporting and
      documentation alongside the daily management of its funds —
      without slowing down the rest of the business. Since 2022, Substance
      Lab has built and continued to develop Folio, the internal system that
      today handles reporting, data integration, customer relationships, and
      compliance monitoring for the association."
  ) %>
<% end %>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <%= markdown(<<~MARKDOWN)
      ## From manual Excel reporting to an automated process

      Falcon Invest's customer reports used to be built in Excel &mdash;
      data pulled manually from other reports and entered into the right
      rows. It was error-prone and took time away from the employee
      responsible for reporting, and as Falcon Invest gained more customers,
      the process simply couldn't keep up.

      Folio now fetches and normalizes positions, transactions, exchange
      rates, and fees from Falcon Invest's banking partners every day, and
      generates the reports &mdash; returns, quarterly overviews, taxation
      &mdash; that used to be built by hand.
    MARKDOWN
    %>

    <aside class="factbox pull-right">
      <div class="factbox-body">
        <h2>Who is Falcon Invest?</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="https://falconinvest.dk">Falcon Invest</a> is a publicly
          listed Danish investment association specializing in momentum and
          multi-factor investing, running three actively managed funds
          supervised by the Danish FSA. The association's investment advisor
          is Falcon Fondsmæglerselskab A/S, which also offers individual
          portfolio management.
        </p>
      </div>

      <table class="factbox-table">
        <tr>
          <th>Website</th>
          <td><a href="https://falconinvest.dk" title="Falcon Invest">falconinvest.dk</a></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </aside>

    <blockquote class="quote pull-left">
      <p>We're drowning in tasks, so we need automation.</p>
      <div class="author">Louise Lykkegård, Falcon Invest</div>
    </blockquote>

    <%= markdown(<<~MARKDOWN)
      That need has been the throughline of the collaboration, which
      actually goes back to 2015, when Substance Lab built one of Falcon
      Invest's first tools for comparing investment models. Every new piece
      of automation in Folio frees up time employees would otherwise spend
      on repeated, manual work.

      ## One normalized data flow across banks

      Folio started as a narrow integration with a single banking partner.
      As Falcon Invest began onboarding customers who banked elsewhere, it
      became clear that a solution built for one data format wouldn't hold
      up.
    MARKDOWN
    %>

    <blockquote class="quote pull-right">
      <p>
        I know we're not quite there yet, but we're far enough along that I
        can see you're once again delivering über cool work as always. It's
        going to save us a lot of time and risk of errors.
      </p>
      <div class="author">René Engell, Portfolio Manager / Investment Director &amp; Partner, Falcon Invest</div>
    </blockquote>

    <%= markdown(<<~MARKDOWN)
      Rather than build a bespoke integration per bank, Folio was expanded
      into a proper ETL process, where data from every provider is
      normalized into Falcon Invest's internal data model, regardless of
      source format. It was a hard transition to build the first time
      &mdash; but the third banking connection was added with surprisingly
      little effort, because the reporting and CRM core didn't need to
      change.

      ## From reporting to CRM and ongoing compliance

      As needs grew, Folio has been extended to also serve as a CRM for
      customer relationships and to manage complex workflows like gradual
      customer onboarding: when a new customer starts with a larger amount
      of capital, Falcon Invest spreads the initial investment out over
      time to diversify the timing of purchases &mdash; a process that can
      involve several currencies and trade windows, which Folio now tracks
      and reminds the responsible people about.

      The system also continuously monitors that customer account balances
      match the agreements in place. That catches discrepancies along the
      way, instead of only surfacing them during the quarterly reporting
      crunch, when the time window is shortest and the pressure highest.

      ## Ownership without vendor lock-in

      Folio is built on mature, open source technologies. That means
      Falcon Invest has full ownership of the code and isn't locked to a
      single vendor &mdash; an important priority for an association that
      has to document and account for its systems to regulators.
    MARKDOWN
    %>

    <blockquote class="quote pull-left">
      <p>
        Best in class! The most skilled developer I've ever worked with.
        Thanks to good architecture, new features and requests get
        implemented very quickly.
      </p>
      <div class="author">Rasmus Sommerskov, Partner, Falcon Management A/S</div>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

